# E-Commerce Data Warehouse Naming Conventions

## Python Files and Classes
- Python modules MUST use snake_case (e.g., generate_customers.py, transform_orders.py)
- Python classes MUST use PascalCase (e.g., CustomerGenerator, OrderTransformer)
- Python functions MUST use snake_case (e.g., generate_customer_data, clean_dataframe)
- Python variables MUST use snake_case (e.g., customer_id, order_date)
- Python constants MUST use UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (e.g., BATCH_SIZE, MAX_RETRIES)

## Database Objects
- Database tables MUST use snake_case (e.g., dim_customer, fact_orders)
- Database columns MUST use snake_case (e.g., customer_id, order_date)
- Primary keys MUST follow pattern: table_name_id (e.g., customer_id, product_id)
- Foreign keys MUST follow pattern: referenced_table_name_id (e.g., customer_id, product_id)
- Surrogate keys MUST use: sk_table_name (e.g., sk_customer, sk_product)

## Airflow Objects
- DAG IDs MUST use snake_case with prefix 'ecommerce_' (e.g., ecommerce_etl_dag, ecommerce_data_quality_dag)
- Task IDs MUST use snake_case (e.g., generate_customers, transform_orders)
- Airflow variables MUST use snake_case with prefix 'ecommerce_' (e.g., ecommerce_data_path, ecommerce_spark_config)

## Spark Objects
- DataFrame variables MUST use snake_case with _df suffix (e.g., customers_df, orders_df)
- Spark configurations MUST use snake_case (e.g., spark_config, parquet_options)
- Temporary views MUST use snake_case with _temp suffix (e.g., orders_temp, customers_temp)

## File Paths and Directories
- Directory names MUST use snake_case (e.g., raw_data, cleaned_data, curated_data)
- File names MUST use snake_case with appropriate extensions (e.g., customers_2023.csv, orders_2023.parquet)
- Partition directories MUST follow pattern: column_name=value (e.g., year=2023, country=US)

## SQL Objects
- SQL table names MUST use snake_case (e.g., dim_customer, fact_orders)
- SQL column names MUST use snake_case (e.g., customer_name, order_amount)
- SQL views MUST use snake_case with _v suffix (e.g., customer_orders_v, product_revenue_v)
- SQL stored procedures MUST use snake_case with _sp suffix (e.g., calculate_ltv_sp, update_dimensions_sp)

## Configuration and Environment
- Environment variables MUST use UPPER_SNAKE_CASE with prefix 'ECOMMERCE_' (e.g., ECOMMERCE_SPARK_MASTER, ECOMMERCE_DATA_LAKE_PATH)
- Configuration keys MUST use snake_case (e.g., spark_master, data_lake_path)
- Log levels MUST use UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (e.g., INFO, DEBUG, ERROR)